tw-pubconnector is easiest to understand as a set of connected research workflows rather than a collection of separate utilities.

!! Authoring and metadata sync

* Treat tiddlers tagged `Colleague` as author profiles.
* Pull works from ORCID, OpenAlex, Google Scholar, Web of Science, and Scopus.
* Cache retrieved data so repeated requests are cheaper and rate-limit friendly.
* Reuse DOI lookups to connect imported literature with existing colleague tiddlers.

!! Literature import and article reading

* Import BibTeX into `bibtex-entry` tiddlers through PubConnector-assisted workflows.
* Upload publisher HTML, typically saved with SingleFile, and match it back to a paper by DOI.
* Open a cleaned article page at `/literature/article/<title>`.
* Highlight text, attach notes, review notes later, and adjust font size while reading.
* Auto-link domain terms in article text back to wiki tiddlers with configurable filters and aliases.

!! Discovery widgets and citation watch

* Show the latest literature added to your wiki.
* Pull references and citing papers for DOI-backed items.
* Review saved highlight notes from a paper without reopening the article first.
* Track recent citations for watched papers or colleagues using Citation Watch.

